  "summary": "Bypasses the `std::locale(\"\")` check in `SetupEnvironment()` when building on illumos-based platforms. This prevents node startup crashes caused by an upstream libstdc++ bug in certain illumos GCC toolchains.",
  "problem": "On illumos-based distributions like OmniOS or OpenIndiana where GCC is built with `--enable-clocale=dragonfly`, `std::ctype<char>::~ctype()` passes an uninitialized pointer to `freelocale()`. As a result, instantiating `std::locale(\"\")` during initialization intermittently crashes Bitcoin Core on startup with memory corruption errors.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit description: 'Constructing and destroying `std::locale(\"\")` in `SetupEnvironment()` therefore intermittently crashes, e.g. with \"libc thread failure: lfree() called with a misaligned pointer\"'.",
    "Links upstream tracking issues in GCC for illumos (illumos/gcc#56), omnios-build#4253, and illumos bug #18481."
  ],
